      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a really powerful framing. I love the idea that the tragedy isn't the choice, but the isolation of the person making it. \n\nCan we actually write out the dialogue for this? I want to see the Senator's specific arguments—make them feel like he's laying out the undeniable, heavy math of national security that just can't be argued away. And for the activist, I want her to hit those big, emotional beats about \"freedom\" and \"human rights,\" but I want the dialogue to reflect that her position is a bit more of a dream than a functional policy. I want the audience to feel that while her heart is in the right place, he's the one actually dealing with the consequences of the real world.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
